1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,879
Email sign-in: missing,
old and rejected codes.

2
00:00:03,879 --> 00:00:08,904
Recover from wrong or expired email
codes, use the newest message,

3
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:13,112
and switch methods when
email cannot be delivered.

4
00:00:14,698 --> 00:00:17,605
After your password,
choose Email me a code.

5
00:00:17,605 --> 00:00:22,564
A sent message appears with the
masked address and the code lifetime.

6
00:00:25,214 --> 00:00:27,490
Email can take a minute or two.

7
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:31,088
Check junk or spam, and
check the masked address.

8
00:00:31,088 --> 00:00:34,572
Never send a verification code to support.

9
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:40,554
If you mistype a code, MERIT explains the
error and shows how many attempts remain.

10
00:00:40,554 --> 00:00:43,456
Read the message before trying again.

11
00:00:43,817 --> 00:00:46,287
An expired code cannot sign you in.

12
00:00:46,287 --> 00:00:52,003
Choose Send a new code after the resend
countdown; repeated clicks will not speed

13
00:00:52,003 --> 00:00:53,308
up delivery.

14
00:00:53,608 --> 00:00:58,817
Wait until Send a new code is
available, then ask for another message.

15
00:00:58,817 --> 00:01:02,194
Use only the code from the newest email.

16
00:01:02,549 --> 00:01:05,724
Requesting another code
replaces the previous one.

17
00:01:05,724 --> 00:01:10,125
This example requests a newer
message after the next countdown.

18
00:01:26,863 --> 00:01:30,728
An older email no longer works
after a newer code is sent.

19
00:01:30,728 --> 00:01:35,193
Use the newest message even if
the older email arrives later.

20
00:01:35,549 --> 00:01:38,680
Too many wrong entries
can also close a code.

21
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:44,158
Instead of continuing to guess, get
a new code or use your authenticator.

22
00:01:44,519 --> 00:01:49,321
Use your authenticator app instead
returns to the other verification method.

23
00:01:49,321 --> 00:01:52,501
Enter its current code
to finish signing in.

24
00:01:52,864 --> 00:01:58,094
If MERIT cannot send the email, it shows
a delivery error and support reference.

25
00:01:58,094 --> 00:02:02,808
Keep that reference when contacting
support, rather than any code.

26
00:02:05,702 --> 00:02:09,400
Choose Try sending again
after a delivery failure.

27
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:15,716
If email remains unavailable, use your
authenticator or an unused recovery code.

28
00:02:16,071 --> 00:02:19,204
An agency can withdraw email-code access.

29
00:02:19,204 --> 00:02:25,699
In that case, the email option disappears;
your authenticator remains the way to sign

30
00:02:25,699 --> 00:02:27,099
in.

31
00:02:31,644 --> 00:02:35,958
In this video you recognized
wrong, expired and replaced codes,

32
00:02:35,958 --> 00:02:41,711
requested a new code after the countdown,
and recovered from delivery failures using

33
00:02:41,711 --> 00:02:43,138
another method.
